USAGE: psinode database [OPTIONS]

Options:
  --proof-timeout-ms arg (=200)         Maximum proof-admission CPU time in 
                                        milliseconds (default 200; independent 
                                        of objective block CPU)
  -p [ --producer ] name                Name of this producer
  -k [ --key ] arg                      A private key to use for block 
                                        production
  --passphrase-file arg                 A file containing a passphrase used to 
                                        encrypt secrets
  -l [ --listen ] endpoint              TCP or local socket endpoint on which 
                                        the server accepts connections
  --mount hostpath[:mountpath]          Makes files available to services
  --database-template arg               Template to install when initializing a
                                        new database
  --database-cache-policy arg (=disabled)
                                        Generic psitri cache policy. This 
                                        candidate supports disabled: read 
                                        promotion off, pinned-cache budget 0 
                                        MiB. Performance qualification is 
                                        pending.
  --tls-trustfile path                  A list of trusted Certification 
                                        Authorities in PEM format
  --tls-cert path                       The file containing the server's 
                                        certificate in PEM format
  --tls-key path                        The file containing the private key 
                                        corresponding to --tls-cert in PEM 
                                        format
  --pkcs11-module path                  Path to a PKCS #11 module to load
  --http-timeout seconds                The maximum time for HTTP clients to 
                                        send or receive a message
  --service-threads num                 The number of threads that run async 
                                        actions posted by services
  -h [ --help ]                         Show this message
  -V [ --version ]                      Print version information

